  ($t$1916$t$, $t$Ogdensburg Borough$t$, $t$SUSSEX$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: NJ Department of Community Affairs, Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (state-enforced; State LEA for Ogdensburg) (NJ DCA, state)","Contact: Louis Kilmer, Fire Official of record for Ogdensburg (NJ Division of Fire Safety), per the state directory · 609-633-6132 · BFCECodeAdmin@dca.nj.gov","Apply: State fee tiers count business days between the Division's receipt and the closing date: more than ten business days for the lowest fee. If the change of occupant does not happen within 6 months, a new application is needed (per the DCA form).","How to apply: Apply online through the NJ DCA Fire Safety Service Portal (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov): choose Apply for an Application, then Apply for Smoke Certification, fill in the data and pay. Help: BFCECodeAdmin@dca.nj.gov or 609-633-6132. The older DCA paper form goes to PO Box 809, Trenton, NJ 08625-0809 with a check payable to Treasurer, State of New Jersey.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 2/1/2019: Louis Kilmer · (609) 633-6132","Smoke detector on each level of the dwelling, including basements, excluding attic or crawl space (DCA form)","Smoke detector and carbon monoxide alarm outside each separate sleeping area, within 10 feet of bedrooms (DCA form)","All smoke detectors and CO alarms in working order; AC powered or interconnected alarms in homes built after January 1977 must be kept working (DCA form)","Fire extinguisher (form still lists it; dropped from the state requirement in February 2025 by P.L.2025, c.19)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"State smoke/CO certificate, applied more than 10 business days before closing","amount":"$45"},{"label":"State smoke/CO 